    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Math was always a struggle for me, especially since my education didn’t go beyond a vocational diploma. My parents didn’t emphasize it much, and I found it too rigid for my creative side. I prefer hands-on subjects like computer science, where I can see practical applications. It’s not that I dislike math entirely—I just never felt it clicked for me, and that frustration stuck over the years. I avoid it when I can, but I respect its importance in certain fields.",
